invariant: INV-56
file: mlkem.c
catches: test/wycheproof.sh
reason: encryption draws e2 under nonce 6, ML-KEM-768's, where FIPS 203
  gives 2k, 8 at ML-KEM-1024. Encapsulation and the re-encryption inside
  decapsulation draw the same wrong noise, so every round trip still
  agrees, and only known answers see it: Wycheproof's ML-KEM-1024 cases
  fail, while the ML-KEM-768 ones, where 2k is 6, pass.

--- old
    mlk_sample_cbd(&noise, coins, (uint8_t)(2 * MLKEM_K)); // e2
--- new
    mlk_sample_cbd(&noise, coins, (uint8_t)6); // e2
